axolotlextras.section.radar=Radar
axolotlextras.radar=Radar
axolotlextras.radar.tooltip=A minimap on the HUD with every player around you shown by the face of their skin, framed in their team colour. NPCs are skipped. Move it in AxolotlClient's HUD editor (the "Radar" box there); size and look are set below.
axolotlextras.radarRange=Radar Range
axolotlextras.radarRange.tooltip=How many blocks the edge of the radar stands for.
axolotlextras.range.16=16 blocks
axolotlextras.radarShape=Radar Shape
axolotlextras.radarShape.tooltip=Round or square.
axolotlextras.radarShape.circle=Circle
axolotlextras.radarShape.square=Square
axolotlextras.radarSize=Radar Size
axolotlextras.radarSize.tooltip=The width and height of the radar, in GUI pixels.
axolotlextras.radarIconSize=Face Size
axolotlextras.radarIconSize.tooltip=The size of the faces on the radar (100% is 10 GUI pixels).
axolotlextras.radarOpacity=Background Opacity
axolotlextras.radarOpacity.tooltip=How dark the radar's background is. 0% leaves only the rim.
axolotlextras.radarRotate=Turn With View
axolotlextras.radarRotate.tooltip=On: the radar turns with you, so ahead of you is always up. Off: north is always up, and a small arrow shows where you look.
axolotlextras.radarSelf=Show Own Face
axolotlextras.radarSelf.tooltip=Your own face in the middle of the radar. Off: a white arrow instead.
axolotlextras.radarTeammates=Radar: Show Teammates
axolotlextras.radarTeammates.tooltip=The radar also shows your teammates (off: enemies only). ESP has its own switch.
axolotlextras.radarInvisible=Radar: Show Invisible
axolotlextras.radarInvisible.tooltip=The radar also shows players with the invisibility effect, faded. ESP, tracers and nametags have their own switch (ESP: Show Invisible).
axolotlextras.radarEdge=Keep Far Players on Edge
axolotlextras.radarEdge.tooltip=Players out of range stay on the edge of the radar, faded, in their direction. Off: they are left out.
axolotlextras.radarBorder=Team Colour Frame
axolotlextras.radarBorder.tooltip=A frame in the team colour around each face.
axolotlextras.radarNames=Show Names
axolotlextras.radarNames.tooltip=The name under each face, at half size.
axolotlextras.radarHeight=Height Arrows
axolotlextras.radarHeight.tooltip=A green arrow next to players more than 3 blocks above you, a red one for players more than 3 blocks below.
axolotlextras.radarGrid=Grid and North
axolotlextras.radarGrid.tooltip=Cross lines, a ring at half the range, and an N on the edge pointing north.
key.axolotlextras.dynamicFov=Toggle Dynamic FOV
dynamicFov.tooltip=On: the view widens when you sprint, draw a bow or have Speed, like vanilla. Off: the FOV stays put. This is AxolotlClient's own option. A toggle key is in Controls, section AxolotlClient (unbound until you set it).
axolotlextras.radarCenter=Radar Centre
axolotlextras.radarCenter.tooltip=What the middle of the radar is. You: the players around you. Your Bed: the players around your own bed, with you shown where you are. The bed radar only works while your bed is within your render distance (players further away are not sent to you), so beyond that, or when your bed is not known or is broken, it turns gray and says why.
axolotlextras.radarCenter.player=You
axolotlextras.radarCenter.bed=Your Bed
axolotlextras.radarBedFallback=Back to You When Bed Breaks
axolotlextras.radarBedFallback.tooltip=With Radar Centre on Your Bed: once your bed is broken, the radar centres on you for the rest of the game. The next game starts on your bed again (Radar Centre itself is not changed). Off: the radar stays gray with "No bed".
key.axolotlextras.radarCenter=Radar: You / Your Bed
